ghtening or revert toward Abbott's fundamentals edge.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Greg Abbott (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Texas governor is closer than usual this cycle. Incumbent Greg Abbott holds the structural advantages: a state that leaned Republican by about six points last presidential cycle, a large fundraising edge, and $67 million in the bank against Gina Hinojosa's $3 million. Yet September polling has been strikingly competitive, averaging roughly a two-point Abbott lead, with Marist and Siena surveys showing Hinojosa narrowly ahead and headlines describing a genuine toss-up.\n\nPrediction markets remain skeptical of an upset, pricing Abbott near 74 percent, and expert ratings cluster between Lean R and Likely R. The forecast lands on a narrow Abbott lead with meaningful uncertainty, reflecting the gap between fundamentals and recent surveys.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1819, "margin": -4.27}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2894, "margin": -3.0}]}